# Fedora's flatpak package enables flatpak-add-fedora-repos.service, which adds the Fedora
# Flatpaks remote at boot. Flathub is the system installation's only remote
# (/usr/share/flatpak/remotes.d/flathub.flatpakrepo). systemd applies the presets again on a
# device's first boot; this file sorts before Fedora's, so the unit stays off.
disable flatpak-add-fedora-repos.service
